# A theme whose picture moves. animated-theme.json tiles
# tests/fixtures/animated/moving.gif over the header from the top left: 16 by
# 12, navy (#000080), four frames without end —
#   frame 0  all navy                                     70 ms
#   frame 1  red    (#ff0000) at 1..5, 1..5                0 ms written: played as 100
#   frame 2  lime   (#00ff00) at 6..10, 3..7               70 ms
#   frame 3  yellow (#ffff00) at 10..14, 6..10             70 ms
# each block taken away again by putting back what was under it. The tile
# that begins at x = 688 (16 x 43) lies in the tab strip's empty right end:
# (691,3) is the red block's, (696,5) the lime's, (700,8) the yellow's.
resize 800 600
open data:text/html,<title>Page</title><body style="margin:0;background:white">page

# The clock starts when the picture is first shown.
assert-pixel 691 3 #000080
assert-pixel 696 5 #000080
mark

# Nothing moves before its time.
advance 69
assert-pixel 691 3 #000080
assert-header-paints 0

# Each frame in its turn — the one with no delay written after a tenth of a
# second — and the header alone painted for it: the page is not drawn again.
advance 1
assert-pixel 691 3 #ff0000
advance 100
assert-pixel 691 3 #000080
assert-pixel 696 5 #00ff00
advance 70
assert-pixel 696 5 #000080
assert-pixel 700 8 #ffff00
advance 70
assert-pixel 700 8 #000080
assert-pixel 691 3 #000080
assert-header-paints 4
assert-paints 0

# Round again: the second play begins as the first did.
advance 70
assert-pixel 691 3 #ff0000

# A window that slept does not play back what it missed: eight frames at
# most, then on from now. Eight on from frame 1 is frame 1 again, and its
# tenth of a second starts over.
advance 5000
assert-pixel 691 3 #ff0000
mark
advance 99
assert-pixel 691 3 #ff0000
assert-header-paints 0
advance 1
assert-pixel 696 5 #00ff00
assert-header-paints 1

# With a menu open the whole frame is painted for a tick: a menu may lie
# over the header, and would be painted under.
main-menu
assert-pixel 696 5 #00ff00
mark
advance 70
assert-pixel 700 8 #ffff00
assert-paints 1
assert-header-paints 0
key Escape

# At twice the scale the tile is 32 by 24 device pixels and moves as it did:
# in the tile that begins at x = 672 the red block is 674..683 by 2..11 and
# the lime one 684..693 by 6..15.
scale 2
advance 70
advance 70
assert-pixel 678 6 #ff0000
advance 100
assert-pixel 678 6 #000080
assert-pixel 688 10 #00ff00
